course: dictionary
lesson: 15832
title: Words for everyday clothes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Underpants is a noun, and it is always plural: you wear a pair of underpants, not an underpants. Look at the words around it to work out what it means. «She put on clean underpants before she put on her socks.» Clean and put on tell you it is clothing worn next to the skin.
explain: A long word can be broken into smaller parts. Under means below, and pants are a kind of clothing, so underpants are pants worn under your trousers or skirt. Breaking a word into parts can help you guess its meaning.
explain: Words can also change from place to place. Read the clues in the text. «In the UK, underpants are usually men's or boys' pants; in the US, the word is used for anyone's.» So when a book set in America says «Mia packed her underpants», the context tells you whose they are.
fact: Underpants means a piece of underwear worn under trousers or a skirt.
fact: «Underpants» is plural only, so say «a pair of underpants».
fact: «Clean underpants» means underpants that have been washed and are not dirty.
fact: In the UK, underpants are usually men's or boys' pants; in the US, the word is used for anyone's.
fact: Health lessons teach that the parts covered by underpants are private, which is the «pants rule».
exercise: «Mum bought me a new pair of underpants for school.» What are underpants? | A hat worn in the rain | A pair of socks worn on the feet | A coat for cold winter days | *A piece of underwear worn under trousers or a skirt
exercise: «Please put on clean underpants before you go to bed.» What does clean mean here? | Very long and loose | *Washed and not dirty | Bright yellow in colour | Full of holes and torn
exercise: Which phrase is correct for one set of underwear? | One underpant | *A pair of underpants | A underpants | An underpants
test: In a US book, «Mia packed her underpants for camp.» Whose underpants could they be? | *Anyone's, including Mia's | Only men's or boys' | Only a dog's | Only the teacher's
test: Why do health lessons talk about the parts covered by underpants? | Because they are ticklish | *Because those parts are private, as the pants rule teaches | Because they must always be shown | Because they are the biggest part of the body
exam: Why do children laugh at the title «Aliens Love Underpants»? | Because aliens hate underpants | Because it is a maths book | *Because underpants are everyday clothes that make children giggle | Because underpants are a kind of food
